## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of event-driven AWS architectures, video processing workflows, and end-to-end data indexing, with emphasis on security, reliability, and cost optimization.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven orchestration using S3 event notifications and Step Functions
- AWS Elemental MediaConvert for multi-format video processing (MP4, GIF thumbnails)
- DynamoDB indexing with comprehensive video metadata
- Security best practices: IAM least privilege, encryption at rest and in transit, access logging
- Robust error handling: retry mechanisms, dead-letter queues, comprehensive monitoring
- Cost optimization strategies: appropriate resource sizing, storage lifecycle policies, and efficient processing patterns

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Lambda snippet: update DynamoDB after MediaConvert completion
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { jobId, status, output } = event.detail;

  if (status === 'COMPLETE') {
    const params = {
      TableName: process.env.VIDEOS_TABLE,
      Item: {
        videoId: output.videoId,
        sourceKey: output.inputFile,
        thumbnailKey: output.thumbnailPath,
        previewKey: output.mp4Path,
        duration: output.duration,
        encodingQuality: '1080p',
        processedAt: new Date().toISOString()
      }
    };

    await ddb.put(params).promise();
  }
};
```

